        <Document ID="6ABACA60-43BA-4109-BFF3-E9CC4D80FF5D">
            <Title>Module 2 requirements</Title>
            <Text>1. Overview &amp; Objectives
Milestone 2 (M2) represents the first technical execution checkpoint of your Data Science Term Project. Following the approval of your Milestone 1 (M1) Project Proposal, M2 shifts focus from planning to implementation.
In this milestone, your team will demonstrate that you have successfully acquired your target dataset, performed thorough data cleaning and preprocessing, conducted initial Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA), and produced meaningful initial data visualizations.
Primary Objectives:
	•	Data Ingestion &amp; Pipeline: Import raw dataset(s) into Python and handle initial data parsing.
	•	Data Cleaning &amp; Preprocessing: Identify and resolve missing values, improper data types, duplicate records, structural inconsistencies, or invalid entries.
	•	Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA): Compute summary metrics, distributions, and descriptive statistics across key variables.
	•	Data Visualization: Create at least two (2) clear, well-labeled visualizations (using matplotlib or standard Python visualization tools) that illuminate distributions or relationships within your data.
	•	Progress Reflection: Evaluate your technical progress against the goals outlined in your M1 proposal and refine your execution plan for Milestone 3 (M3).

2. Required Deliverables
Each team (1 to 3 members) must submit a single compressed archive (.zip) or GitHub repository link on Canvas containing the following three deliverables:
Deliverable A: Cleaned Data Pipeline &amp; Analysis Code
	•	A clean, well-structured, executable Python script (m2_analysis.py) or Jupyter Notebook (m2_analysis.ipynb).
	•	The script/notebook must execute without errors from top to bottom.
	•	Include inline comments and docstrings explaining data cleaning decisions and processing steps.
Deliverable B: Cleaned Dataset or Reproducible Data Generation Script
	•	The processed, clean dataset exported as a standardized file format (e.g., .csv or .json), OR
	•	A reproducible data cleaning function/script that automatically transforms raw input data into the cleaned format.
Deliverable C: Milestone 2 Progress Report
	•	A written progress document (2–4 pages or ~1,000–1,500 words) structured into the five required report sections detailed below.
	•	Link to shared Google Doc or Word 365 file or .pdf or Word .docx file.
	•	Can use Milestone 2 — Data Cleaning &amp; Exploration Progress Report TemplateLinks to an external site. as a template.

3. M2 Progress Report Structure
Your written M2 report must include the following explicit section headers:
1. Executive Summary &amp; Proposal Alignment
2. Data Acquisition &amp; Preprocessing
3. Exploratory Data Analysis &amp; Summary Statistics
4. Initial Data Visualizations &amp; Insights
5. Challenges Encountered &amp; Next Steps for M3
Section Details:
1. Executive Summary &amp; Proposal Alignment
	•	Provide a brief recap of your project's primary problem statement, domain, and core research questions as defined in M1.
	•	Briefly summarize what was accomplished during this milestone phase.
2. Data Acquisition &amp; Preprocessing
	•	Dataset Characteristics: Specify source URL, original file format, row count, column count, and variable data types.
	•	Cleaning Workflow: Detail all preprocessing steps applied to the dataset:
	•	Handling missing, null, or corrupt values (e.g., filtering, dropping, or imputing).
	•	Data type conversions (e.g., converting string dates or numbers to proper int/float/datetime types).
	•	Renaming headers, removing duplicate records, or filtering out invalid outliers.
3. Exploratory Data Analysis &amp; Summary Statistics
	•	Present core descriptive statistics for key quantitative and qualitative variables:
	•	Quantitative variables: Count, mean, median, standard deviation, minimum, maximum.
	•	Qualitative/Categorical variables: Unique categories, category frequency counts, mode.
	•	Discuss initial trends, patterns, or anomalies observed in the processed dataset.
4. Initial Data Visualizations &amp; Insights
	•	Include at least two (2) original visualizations generated using matplotlib (e.g., histograms, scatter plots, bar charts, box plots).
	•	Every figure must include:
	•	Descriptive figure title
	•	Clearly labeled axes with appropriate units
	•	Legend (where applicable)
	•	A 1–2 paragraph narrative explaining what the plot demonstrates and its relevance to your core project questions.
5. Challenges Encountered &amp; Next Steps for M3
	•	Document technical obstacles encountered during data cleaning or script development and how you addressed them.
	•	State any necessary adjustments made to your project scope or methodology since M1.
	•	Detail the team's planned execution goals for Milestone 3 (M3) (e.g., advanced statistical modeling, feature engineering, complex visualizations, or algorithm implementation).

4. Code Standards &amp; Technical Expectations
Your Python code will be evaluated on technical accuracy, defensive programming, and code quality.
	•	Modularity: Utilize custom functions (def) to encapsulate data cleaning logic and data analysis tasks.
	•	Defensive Guard Logic: Ensure code handles edge cases gracefully (e.g., checking for empty collections or division by zero using standard built-ins like len()).
	•	Standard Library &amp; Tool Usage:
	•	Base data structures: list, dict, tuple, set.
	•	Standard math &amp; stats: math, statistics, random.
	•	Scientific/Data libraries (as covered in Weeks 11–12): numpy, matplotlib.pyplot.
	•	PEP 8 Guidelines: Maintain readable code formatting, consistent variable naming (snake_case), and appropriate whitespace/indentation.

5. Evaluation &amp; Grading Rubric
Milestone 2 is graded out of 100 Points Total, allocated across technical execution, analysis quality, visualization, and documentation:
Evaluation Criteria
Points
Description
Data Cleaning &amp; Pipeline Execution
30 pts
Dataset successfully imported and cleaned. Null values, data types, and formatting errors correctly addressed with reproducible Python code.
Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
25 pts
Comprehensive summary statistics computed for key variables. Logic demonstrates strong computational understanding of data structures.
Data Visualization Quality
20 pts
At least 2 clear, professional matplotlib plots provided with proper titles, axis labels, and explanatory narratives.
Written Report &amp; Reflection
15 pts
Clear documentation following all 5 required sections, thoroughly explaining progress, technical challenges, and roadmap for M3.
Code Structure &amp; Formatting
10 pts
Code adheres to PEP 8 standards, contains modular functions, runs without execution errors, and includes descriptive comments.
Total Base Score
100 pts
</Text>
        </Document>
